## Context

Child of tickets/0205. Re-scoped 2026-06-05 (ACP/A2A dig): instead of
one bespoke adapter per reviewer kind, the management surface is ONE
Agent Client Protocol (ACP) client harness driving N interchangeable
seats. The client mediates all filesystem and terminal access in ACP,
so the harness grants each seat fs/read only — no fs/write, no
terminal — and the 0193/0202 drift catalog becomes structurally
impossible for every seat, not prompt-discouraged. Adding a reviewer =
adding a roster stanza, not writing an adapter. Seats available day
one: Gemini CLI and Copilot CLI (native ACP), 0207's thin model agent
(OpenRouter / llama-server), and claude-code-acp as the sibling-tier
Claude seat (keeps subscription auth — no funded API key). The seats
never run tests; the orchestrator runs them and feeds results into
each seat's prompt context. Helpers are tool-named where they wrap one
tool (0205 naming exception); the umbrella skill itself is generic.

## Relevant files

- new: skills/reviewers/SKILL.md + the ACP client harness helper
  (pure I/O; spawns a seat sub-process, speaks JSON-RPC over stdio)
- new: reviewer roster config (one place: seat = {agent_cmd, model,
  kind, status advisory|required}; no secrets — credentials via
  BASH_ENV path, see 0207)
- skills/verify/SKILL.md — calls into this instead of inlining mechanics
- tickets/0206, tickets/0207 — the reviewers being managed

## Actions

1. ACP client harness: spawn the seat's agent_cmd, initialize with
   capabilities {fs/read: yes, fs/write: NO, terminal: NO}, session/new,
   session/prompt with the review directive (diff, ticket, test results,
   0205 contract shape), stream session/update into a findings file,
   deny any session/request_permission for mutation. One harness, every
   seat.
2. `/reviewers list` — panel roster, each seat's kind, advisory/required
   status, trial progress (MRs observed / projects covered).
3. `/reviewers request <pr>` — fire all configured seats for a merge
   request (ACP sessions; plus the 0206 forge-bot request, the one
   non-ACP member while it lasts).
4. `/reviewers harvest <pr>` — collect all findings, normalize to the
   0205 contract shape, emit one findings file for the gate.
5. `/reviewers scorecard <pr> <verdict-summary>` — append the per-MR
   trial line to the owning ticket's log (the 0206/0207 observation
   bookkeeping, mechanized).
6. Config lives in one place (the roster); no secrets in config —
   credentials via BASH_ENV path (see 0207).

## Test

Shell test with a stub ACP agent on PATH (canned JSON-RPC responses) +
stubbed forge CLI: harness grants exclude fs/write and terminal;
`request` opens one session per configured seat; a stub
session/request_permission for a write is DENIED; `harvest` merges two
stub finding files into one normalized output; `scorecard` appends a
valid erg log line (verbs: created/note/closed only) that `erg
validate` accepts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] ACP client harness: one client, N seats, fs/read-only grants, mutation permission requests denied
- [ ] /reviewers skill with list/request/harvest/scorecard, catalog-registered
- [ ] verify's panel-extension section delegates mechanics to it
- [ ] Stubbed shell test green; make check green
